            "content": "Geneva",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.091,
                0.246,
                0.243,
                0.262
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Sixteenth session",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.091,
                0.277,
                0.236,
                0.291
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "20–23 October 2025",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph_title",
            "bbox": [
                0.186,
                0.354,
                0.785,
                0.391
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "The Geneva Consensus for a just and sustainable economic order: Political declaration"
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.185,
                0.406,
                0.812,
                0.45
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "We, the member States of the United Nations Conference on Trade and Development (UNCTAD), gathered in Geneva, Switzerland, from 20 to 23 October 2025 for the sixteenth session of the Conference, agree on the following declaration.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.184,
                0.456,
                0.813,
                0.542
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "1. We endorse and support the consensual outcome document of the Conference. The document outlines our shared priorities for trade and development, reaffirms the UNCTAD mandate and gives guidelines for the work of the organization in the coming four years through its three pillars of consensus-building, research and analysis and technical assistance in the areas of finance, science and technology, investments and sustainable development.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.184,
                0.548,
                0.813,
                0.634
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "2. We value the UNCTAD contribution to an equitable and inclusive international trading system based on rules and appreciate the role of the organization in the establishment of scientific evidence in economic affairs. We commend the function of UNCTAD as the global platform for dialogue on trade and development and recognize the contribution of the organization to the implementation of the Sustainable Development Goals.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.184,
                0.64,
                0.813,
                0.728
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "3. We note with appreciation that we are meeting in the Assembly Hall of the Palais des Nations in Geneva, the very same place where UNCTAD was created in 1964, and recognize it as a powerful reminder of the historic commitment of our countries to multilateral cooperation for development. Since the establishment of UNCTAD sixty-one years ago, our countries have worked together to reduce development gaps between us by promoting trade, investments and economic cooperation.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.184,
                0.734,
                0.813,
                0.806
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "4. From a historical perspective, we acknowledge that we have succeeded in implementing development policies that have borne fruit in several areas. Simultaneously, we are conscious that our common objective of a world where prosperity, social development and well-being are equitably shared by countries and peoples is not yet achieved, requiring renewed commitment and solidarity to ensure no one is left behind.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.184,
                0.812,
                0.813,
                0.914
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "5. We value the rich exchanges we had during the sixteenth session of the Conference under the theme of “Shaping the future: Driving economic transformation for equitable, inclusive and sustainable development”. The Conference enabled us to agree on the fact that the global economic order is confronted with major shocks and crises and that it has entered a phase of transition marked by both destabilizing uncertainties and promising opportunities. To prepare for the future in this challenging context and changing environment, we agree on a new consensus for a just and sustainable economic order by",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
